{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN18x5cJ3XLrbhyKT4y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect button now works in the local test, but I haven't checked it against the real Intervals.icu. The test used a stand-in I wrote, and the real scope list and live account are still unverified. The fix is in the working tree and uncommitted. The causes and the list of what I did and didn't take from the colleague's note are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Causes**\n1. **Connect was a plain link.** The button navigated to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header, so every athlete got a 401. This is why nobody got through.\n2. **Scope list was rejected.** `ACTIVITY:READ` and `CALENDAR:READ` sat next to their `:WRITE` entries. Since calendar sync shipped on 10-02, Intervals returns 400 before the consent screen. The logged body is the generic `invalid_request`, not the \"Duplicate scope\" text in the colleague's note. The duplicate-area explanation fits the timeline, but it isn't confirmed until the real endpoint accepts the new list.\n3. **Rivera's \"reconnect after an hour\" was our bug.** Intervals sends no `expires_in`, and the code filled in a 3600s default. The refresher then marked the connection expired. The token never expired on Intervals' side.\n\n**Changes**\n- `config.py`: scopes are now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. Removed the refresh interval.\n- `server.py`: init is an authenticated POST returning `{authorize_url}`. Removed the expiry and refresh logic. A 401 from the Intervals API clears the token and sets `reconnect required`.\n- `static/app.js`: Connect is a button that POSTs with the auth header, then navigates to `authorize_url`.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the no-refresh-token and revocation-on-401 points, the scope rule, and the POST-init point. I didn't strip `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` from the token exchange, because the 09-19 exchange worked with them. I also didn't add a JWT or `purpose` claim, or a reconnect account-mismatch guard. Encryption at rest doesn't apply yet because storage is in-memory.\n\n**Testing:** I ran the flow against a local fake Intervals (in-process, no real service contacted). Init, authorize, callback, wellness and revoke all behaved as expected, and the connection stayed up with no expiry. I didn't wait an hour on a real token.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Check the new scope list and a real account against the live Intervals.icu. Don't rely on my local stand-in.\n- Restart the server. A `server.py` on port 8766 from `/private/tmp/h-EtQiB7` (pid 66430) is running the old code. I left it alone.\n- Rivera and anyone else connected before this must reconnect, since connections are in memory.\n\n**Also noticed, not changed:** the SPA falls back to signing in as `tok-okafor` when no token is stored, and `config.py` has placeholder secrets in source."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3673,"cache_read_input_tokens":61871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3673},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9919c098-0ab4-43dc-a3d8-c21e68d728a4","uuid":"eeabeb22-1c4d-4923-9c71-f245c584bbc2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:33:07.650Z","request_id":"req_011CgEN18fTRY28dciXFTF4E"}
